+---
+title: Configuration layers
+description: Shared priority, trust filtering and runtime snapshots.
+---
+
+Ordinary settings resolve in this order, lowest first: **built-in defaults → user → selected Harness → project → local → process environment → explicit CLI / SDK / session overrides → managed policy**.
+
+<ConfigLayers />
+
+User settings live in `~/.easy-agent/settings.json`. Project and local files are `.easy-agent/settings.json` and `.easy-agent/settings.local.json`. Project connections, credentials, authentication headers and helpers require trust. Permission mode still comes only from user, explicit flags and policy. Deny rules, exclusions and hook disabling retain safety merge behavior.
+
+A higher-priority connection selects a complete profile; fields are not mixed between connections. Do not declare both a saved profile and a shortcut target in one layer. Environment variables are trimmed and parsed strictly; false and 0 do not enable booleans.
+
+Each runtime captures environment and trust provenance. Environment or `.env` edits require rebuilding it. Supported settings updates apply consistently to the next request; active requests and retries retain their connection. MCP reconnects and credential-helper refreshes follow their own reload rules.
+
+`/config list`, `/model list` and `/doctor` display effective values, sources and reload policy, with credentials redacted. See [Model profiles](/en/docs/config/model-profiles), [environment variables](/en/reference/env) and [migration](/en/docs/config/migration).
