@@ -0,0 +1,40 @@
+---
+title: Configuration migration and rollback
+description: Preview differences, resolve conflicts and retain exact private backups.
+---
+
+**This upgrade is a breaking configuration change.** Runtime accepts canonical configuration only. Retired fields and unreferenced retired environment variables report errors. Startup and ordinary saves never convert them. Settings remain accessible; conversion is available only through the explicit migration command/API.
+
+```bash
+eagent config migrate --scope user --json
+eagent config migrate --scope user --apply
+```
+
+The desktop Models page previews before **Back up and apply**. SDK exposes `previewConfigMigration(scope)` / `applyConfigMigration(scope, revision)`; RPC exposes `config/migrationPreview` / `config/migrationApply`. Scopes are user/project/local. Preview executes no helper or model request and redacts secrets. Conflicts prevent apply; a changed file or runtime requires another preview.
+
+| Retired input | Canonical handling |
+|---|---|
+| `ANTHROPIC_API_KEY`, `ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN` | One EASY_AGENT_API_KEY and a confirmed explicit Anthropic connection |
+| `ANTHROPIC_MODEL`, `ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL` | EASY_AGENT_MODEL / EASY_AGENT_BASE_URL with an explicit protocol |
+| `defaultModel`, raw model selections | Stable profile ID under model; preserve the actual old choice without upgrading it |
+| Global `apiKeyHelper` | apiKey helper belonging to one unambiguous profile |
+| Authentication headers | One API Key and explicit authentication; conflicting secrets block apply |
+| `countTokens`, `promptCacheKey` | Selected protocolOptions, preserving true and false |
+| `alwaysThinkingEnabled`, old thinking features, `MAX_THINKING_TOKENS` | reasoning.mode / budgetTokens; old zero becomes off |
+| `effortLevel`, `features.effort` | reasoning.effort |
+| Global adaptive/interleaved switches | Selected Anthropic profile options |
+| Force effort for every model | Capability on one applicable profile, never broadcast |
+| CLAUDE_CODE context/retry/beta aliases | Existing canonical EASY_AGENT variables |
+| `WEB_SEARCH_ADAPTER`, `MCP_CONNECT_TIMEOUT` | EASY_AGENT_WEB_SEARCH_BACKEND / EASY_AGENT_MCP_CONNECT_TIMEOUT_MS |
+| Old ToolSearch variables | Settings or CLI |
+| `claudeMdExcludes` | agentMdExcludes, safely unioned with existing exclusions |
+
+Equal old keys merge; different keys block connection migration without revealing either. A complete canonical connection does not borrow old fields. Duplicate default authentication headers are removed; gateways must declare their policy explicitly. A variable named Token does not imply Bearer. See the [complete mapping](https://github.com/ConardLi/easy-agent/blob/main/docs/configuration-migration.md).
+
+These conversions happen only during explicit migration. Residual old variables block model requests even with a complete canonical profile; remove them and rebuild the runtime. Explicit references such as `${ANTHROPIC_API_KEY}` remain valid ordinary environment references. Sessions restore saved profile IDs only; a historical raw model name requires an explicit profile selection even when one upstream-model match exists.
+
+Unknown IDs no longer imply Anthropic models, no fixed model is selected without configuration, unknown automatic reasoning is conservative, and plain ultrathink text does not change settings. False/0 are parsed as false; numeric input is fully validated. Environment priority is below explicit CLI/SDK/session and policy. Trust, permissions, resources and exclusions retain their safety rules.
+
+Apply saves exact original bytes beside the file as `*.pre-standardization-<timestamp>.bak`, private with POSIX 0600 or Windows account ACLs. Canonical migrations are idempotent. Ordinary saves reject retired fields without changing the file or creating a migration backup; explicitly deleting old fields while writing replacements is supported. Shell settings, CI Secrets and external credentials are not changed. Environment edits require a new runtime.
+
+For rollback stop active runtimes, restore the printed backups, install the known-good version recorded before upgrading, and restore any environment changes you made yourself. Keep backups private: they may contain old inline keys. Names retained in diagnostics, the explicit converter, historical tutorials and third-party Skill formats do not enable automatic legacy configuration.
