+---
+title: Model profiles
+description: One connection contract for protocols, credentials, capabilities and role selection.
+---
+
+`models.<id>` defines a connection; `model` selects its stable profile ID. The upstream `model` inside the profile is a separate name.
+
+```json
+{
+  "model": "main",
+  "models": {
+    "main": { "protocol": "openai-chat", "model": "gpt-4.1", "apiKey": "${EASY_AGENT_API_KEY}" },
+    "local": {
+      "protocol": "openai-chat", "model": "qwen3-coder:30b",
+      "baseURL": "http://localhost:11434/v1", "authentication": { "type": "none" }
+    }
+  },
+  "reasoning": { "mode": "auto" }
+}
+```
+
+| Field | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `protocol` | Required: `anthropic`, `openai-chat`, `openai-responses`, `gemini` |
+| `model` | Required upstream model, including gateway names |
+| `baseURL` | Optional address; only the explicit protocol supplies its official default |
+| `apiKey` | One source: explicit environment reference, secure storage reference, or `{ "helper": "command" }` |
+| `authentication` | Protocol default, `{ type: "header", name, prefix? }`, or explicit `{ type: "none" }` |
+| `headers` | Extra non-authentication headers; may reference environment variables |
+| `maxTokens` | Maximum output, distinct from context and reasoning budget |
+| `capabilities` | Tools, vision, cache, reasoning, effort, contextWindow, maxOutputTokens and optional pricing overrides |
+| `protocolOptions` | Selected protocol only: Anthropic countTokens/adaptiveThinking/interleavedThinking, OpenAI promptCacheKey |
+
+An unknown profile is an error. One valid profile may be selected automatically; several require a default. With none, configuration and help remain available. Changing a saved profile's address or protocol requires an explicit credential source or no-auth policy; another connection's key is never inherited.
+
+Default authentication uses `x-api-key` for Anthropic, Bearer for OpenAI and `x-goog-api-key` for Gemini. A custom policy still references one API Key. No-auth profiles omit `apiKey`. Shared settings use references. A helper has a 10-second timeout, belongs to its profile and never writes a global credential; failure does not fall back to a different source.
+
+Set referenced environment variables before starting. Provider variable names work through explicit references only. Project connections and helpers require trust; parent credentials cannot be replaced by project environment injection.
+
+Reasoning uses `reasoning.mode: auto|on|off`, optional positive `budgetTokens` and `effort: low|medium|high|max`. Unknown models receive no unconfirmed automatic reasoning or experimental parameters. Context defaults to a labelled 32000-token estimate and pricing stays unknown; capabilities can override them. Output, reasoning and context bounds are jointly validated.
+
+`modelRoles` accepts profile IDs for background, think, longContext, compaction and webFetch. Harness `model.roles.classifier` or `EASY_AGENT_AUTO_MODE_MODEL` selects the Auto Mode classifier. Unset roles inherit the main profile; invalid explicit references fail. See [Connect a model](/en/docs/models) and [migration](/en/docs/config/migration).
