+
+```bash
+eagent [options]
+```
+
+| Option | Meaning |
+|---|---|
+| `--help`, `--version` | Display information without needing a model |
+| `--model <profile-id>` | Select a saved profile; unknown IDs error |
+| `--resume [id]` | Restore the last or named session; credentials are resolved again |
+| `--settings <path>` | Explicit settings layer |
+| `--harness <name-or-file>` | Select an Agent |
+| `--trust-project-config` | Trust the project for this runtime |
+| `--max-turns <n>` | Positive tool-turn limit |
+| `--tool-search off|auto|on` | Tool schema loading |
+| `--agent-teams` | Enable Agent Teams |
+| `--plan`, `--auto`, `--permission-mode` | Permission mode |
+| `--dangerously-skip-permissions` | Explicit headless approval of otherwise undecided calls; deny still applies |
+| `-p`, `--print [prompt]` | Headless text/JSON/stream-json output |
+| `--rpc`, `--acp` | JSON-RPC or editor Agent Client Protocol |
+| `--login` | Select a protocol and create a profile with one API Key |
+| `--dump-system-prompt` | Display the assembled prompt |
+
+```bash
+eagent --model main --plan
+eagent config migrate --scope user --json
+eagent config migrate --scope user --apply
+```
+
+Temporary connections use EASY_AGENT_PROTOCOL, EASY_AGENT_MODEL, optional EASY_AGENT_BASE_URL and EASY_AGENT_API_KEY. EASY_AGENT_PROFILE selects a saved connection. Priority remains below managed policy; environment changes require a new runtime. See [profiles](/en/docs/config/model-profiles) and [migration](/en/docs/config/migration).
